<!--
  Voiid mark — PEACOCK TEAL, FLAT. Three rounded bars forming the V, all VoiidPalette.primary
  (#13828C).

  The lime original shaded the back bar with a five-stop gradient (#457512 at the ends to
  #AAD91E mid-bar), which made that bar read as one stroke passing BEHIND the other two.
  Flattening drops that depth cue deliberately — see the note in public/Voiid logo.svg, which
  this file mirrors shape-for-shape.

  Rotations are BAKED IN: Android vector <path> has no transform attribute, so these path data
  are the SVG's rotated rects resolved into absolute coordinates. Do not "simplify" them back
  into rects; they will not match the iOS and web marks if you do.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="88dp"
    android:height="80dp"
    android:viewportWidth="88"
    android:viewportHeight="80">
